Emergency Service authority shall be liable to pay such fee as maybe prescribed by the State Govemment from time to time in thisbehalf.
(2) The fee relerred to in sub-section (1) shall be patable within onemonth of the service of a notice of demand by the Director on theState Govemment or local body or Fire and Emergency Serviceauthority, as the case may be, and if it is not paid within that period,it shall be recoverable as an arrear of land revenue.
50. Any amount payable under this Act shall be recovered as arrearsof land revenue.
CHAPTER XMISCELLANEOUS51. The Director may, with the previous sanction of the StateGovemment, enter into an agreement with any Fire and EmergencyService or the Authority which maintains the said Fire andEmergency Service, beyond the limits of any area in which this Actis in force for providing personnel or equipment or both, forfirefighting purposes, on such terms as may be provided by or underthe agreement on reciprocal basis in public interest. (See : Scheduleof formats).52. Without prejudice to the provisions of any other law on thesubject for tho time being in force, the State Govemment may, bynotification in the Official Gazette, declare the Fire and EmergencyService as Technical Service.
53. The Director or any Fire Officer authorized by the StateGovemment in this behalf may, on the occasion of a fire or otheremergency in any neighboring area in which this Act is not in force,order the dispatch of the employees of the Fire and EnrergencyService with necessary appliances and equipment to carry out fire-fighting operations in such neighboring area and thereupon all theprovisions olthis Act and the rules made there under shall apply tosuch areas, during the period of fire emergency or during suchperiod as the Director may specify on such charges as may beprescribed from time to time.54. It shall be lawful for the State Goue--eni or any officerauthorized by it in this behall to employ the Fire and EmergencyService in any rescue, salvage or other works for which it is suitableby reason of its training, appliances and equipment.
55. The Director or employees of Fire and Emergency Service,authorized by general or special order in this behalf may, for the
Reciprocalfire-fightingarrangementswith other FireandEmergencyService.
Declaration ofFire andEmergencyService asTechnicalService.
Deployment toother area.
Employmenton otherduties.
