431 0 obj
<</Length 1463
>>
stream
I
STATEMENT OF OBJECTS AND REASONS
The Manipur Fire and Emergency Service Bill, 2026 is to strengthen and modemise the fireand emergency response system in the State. With rapid urbanisation, growth of infrastructure,and emerging fire risks, it has become necessery to update and rationalise the existing firesafety standards.1 . The proposed law seeks to rationalise fire safety norms in line with global benchmarks,modem techlology, and national standards, particularly with regard to fire preventionmeasures, fire protection systems, emergency response, and enforcement mechanisms.It also aims to streamline compliance requirements while ensuring adequate safety inbuildings, industries, and public places.2. The proposed law will help improve public safety, disaster preparedness, and theeffective management of fire and emergency services in the State of Manipur.3. The Manipur Fire and Emergency Service Bill, 2026 will continue to safeguard publicsafety by requiring periodic verification of fire safety measures, while at the same timeminimising avoidable hardship to the public and applicants.4. The proposed law is thus intended to strike a balance between ensuring eflective firesafety measures and promoting compliance reduction and deregulation in line with theEase of Doing Business initiative. The proposed law makes govemment procedureseasier, faster, and more cost-effective for the people of Manipur.Hence, this Bill.
Minister (i/c Home)Manipur

endstream
endobj
