MEMORANDUM ON DELEGATED LEGISLATION
I . Clause 6
Proposed Law empowers the State Govemment to appoint differentposts.
2. Clause 8
Proposed Law empowers the State Govemment to setting up of FireStations.
3
Clause 10
Proposed Law empowers the State Government to augment the Fireand Ernergency Service, it may raise an auxiliary service by enrolmentofvolunteers for such area and on such terms and conditions as it maydeem fit as per rules.
4
Clause 21
Empowers the State Govemment to set up fire preventing and auditwing in the Manipur Fire & Emergency Service which shall consist ofsuch number of inspecting oflicer and other staff.
Clause 45 Empowers the State Govemment to establish training centres and toprescribe fees and procedures as may be provided under this proposedlaw
Clause 53 Empowers the State government to notify and declare the Fire andEmergency Service as Technical Service.Clause 63 Empowers the State Govemment to makes rules in terms ofrecruitment to, and pay and other allowances
The delegations are not excessive and normal in character
5
6
7

